<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#conscription">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Conscription</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as conscript</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Conscription is compulsory enlistment of people into state service, especially the armed forces. Ancient states such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han Dynasty</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> relied on obligatory military service, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a> had its militia system. Modern mass conscription armies were raised by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan">Empire of Japan</a>, and by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> in the world wars.</p></div>
